# R-CM7 R-PH12 R-SC1 R-SC6 R-SC7 R-SC8 R-SC14 R-SC15 R-H4 R-H7 R-C2 R-FL6 R-FL7 R-J1 R-J3 R-J4 R-OUT4 R-EC2 R-EC10 R-E4 R-PD9 (slice 011, Q12 to Q15, Q24, Q25): `tln why` on the real binary. The packages are in the cache (the header URLs keep github.com, nothing is fetched).
# The project is the one of `list/ls1-list`: a platform, `web` (names core 1.0.0 and text 1.0.0), `core` 1.1.0 (raised), `mid` (names text 1.1.0, which wins and names core 1.1.0), a path entry `util` (names core 1.0.0, text 2.0.0 and a path
# entry), and a foreign URL. 2 series of acme/text are in the closure. `tie/` has the design example of R-SC14: the platform roc-lang/basic-webserver as `pf`, and `acme/web-utils`, which names someone/basic-webserver (the alias of the
# design example is `web-utils`, but a header alias has no `-`, so it is `web_utils` here).
st() { echo "== $*"; if "$@"; then echo "exit 0"; else echo "exit $?"; fi; }

# A header alias. core is a direct entry that is raised, and 4 other routes reach it: through web, through web and text, through mid and text, through the path entry util (Q15: `util (path)`). The paths are in the order of the links (Q13).
st tln why core
# A short name that matches one package (R-SC8): the repo name of the platform entry.
st tln why pfx --json
# The path entry (R-H4, Q15) is a package of the closure: a header alias names it.
st tln why util
# 2 series of one repo: the short name and the full name are a tie (R-SC14, R-SC15), the series in the name picks one (Q12 of slice 004).
st tln why acme/text
st tln why acme/text@2
# The design example of R-SC14: 2 packages with the repo name basic-webserver. The full name of the second one is found, and its path is `web_utils -> ws`.
st tln why basic-webserver --file tie/main.roc
st tln why someone/basic-webserver --file tie/main.roc
# A name that is in no closure (P6 of slice 004, Q7 of slice 004). The alias of a package that is not a header entry (`inner`, `ws`) is no alias (R-SC6).
st tln why zzz
st tln why ws --file tie/main.roc
# One name only (Q25: the count is a usage failure). R-FL7: `why` rejects the flags of the commands that resolve.
st tln why
st tln why core web
st tln why core --strategy lowest
# A closure that has no tuple: exit 10 and no answer (R-EC10).
st tln why core --file conflict/main.roc
echo "== the files are not changed"
cat main.roc
